  "default_location": "inside the installed package, which is where the invariance suite expects them; antiSMASH also takes --databases PATH, so for distribution this can be a mount instead of an image layer",
  "description": "Fetched by `download-antismash-databases` at the version above. antiSMASH's pin is this PAIR -- binary plus database release -- because the detection rules and the reference data together decide which regions come out. Recording only the binary version would leave half the pin unrecorded.",
  "detection_rule_fingerprint": "04add3eb0e86a816",
  "detection_rule_fingerprint_note": "sha256 over the three cluster-rule files, truncated to 16 hex characters. 103 rules at this version (90 strict, 7 relaxed, 6 loose), against 88 at v7.1 and 58 at v5 -- which is why a campaign must pin what it was built against rather than trust the version string alone.",
  "fetched_on": "2026-10-02",
  "gigabytes_on_disk": 9.4
 },
 "artifact_bytes": 539273452,
 "banned_binaries": {
  "FastTreeMP": "Deleted from the prefix after install. Thread order affects the neighbour-joining heuristic, so it can never sit on a gold-producing path. It arrives as part of the fasttree package that antiSMASH depends on, so the ban is enforced by `registry --verify` rather than only written down. Single-threaded FastTree stays."
 },
 "channels": [
  "conda-forge",
  "bioconda"
 ],
 "description": "The resolved package set of the Phase 1 pinned-tool image, exactly as micromamba installed it. Every entry carries the artifact URL and its sha256, so the image is rebuildable byte-for-byte rather than merely version-matched. A score is comparable only against a run of the same image, and this file is what makes 'the same image' checkable.",
 "not_in_this_image": {
  "bigscape": "Needed by T-L3-2, and its pin depends on the antiSMASH and pyhmmer versions. It follows antiSMASH, which is now here.",
  "iqtree": "Not needed by any catalogued template. If it ever is: always --seed, always fixed -T N, never AUTO, and single-gene ML trees are not admissible as gold.",
  "matchms": "Needed by T-L4-1 and T-L4-2. Pip-installable, but those rows need an MS2 fixture set from MassBank with its own grounding pass first: for a spectral match the invariance question becomes a tolerance question."
 },
